<article class="env-lemma" id="04VI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04VI">Lemma <span data-tag="04VI">4.27.13</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category and let $S$ be a right multiplicative system of morphisms of $\mathcal{C}$. Given any finite collection $g_ i : X \to Y_ i$ of morphisms of $S^{-1}\mathcal{C}$ (indexed by $i$), we can find an element $s : X' \to X$ of $S$ and a family of morphisms $f_ i : X' \to Y_ i$ of $\mathcal{C}$ such that $g_ i$ is the equivalence class of the pair $(f_ i : X' \to Y_ i, s : X' \to X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma is the dual of Lemma <a href="/tag/04VE" data-tag="04VE">4.27.5</a> and follows formally from that lemma by replacing all categories in sight by their opposites. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>